  paragraphs:
    - "HE INTENSE IN-TENTS SALE IS BACK!"
    - "Every two years, we empty the warehouse, dig through estate leftovers and consigned property, put up the tents—and sell an enormous amount of stuff.. This is our Warehouse & Estate Clean-Out Sale, and it all has to go."
    - "We’re working all weekend hauling things out, unpacking boxes and filling the tents. We honestly don’t know everything we’re going to find yet."
    - "So far, expect:"
    - "• Danish Modern furniture"
    - "• Good art, bad art & everything in between"
    - "• Oriental carpets"
    - "• Books"
    - "• Interesting glass & china"
    - "• An old carousel horse"
    - "• Vintage toys"
    - "• An old hardware-store round nail display cabinet"
    - "• An antique iron book press"
    - "• Old meat scales"
    - "• Furniture, decorative objects, oddities and surprises"
    - "• And SO much more"
    - "This is not one of our carefully curated estate sales. This is the clean-out."
    - "There will be treasures. There will be bargains. There will be things we have no idea why we still own."
    - "We’ll be posting more photos as we unpack and set everything up, so keep checking back—there is much more coming."
